  "id": "affective-ambivalence",
  "term": "affective ambivalence",
  "definition": "Affective ambivalence is a decision-making state in which emotional responses pull preference in a different direction from more deliberate or cognitive evaluation. It refers to conflict between affect and thought when choosing, especially under complex conditions.",
